🔥 5. Most Used Array Methods in Automation + Interview
Let’s go deep into important methods:

✅ push() – Add to end
js
Copy
Edit
const tools = ['Playwright'];
tools.push('Selenium');
console.log(tools); // ['Playwright', 'Selenium']
✅ pop() – Remove last item
js
Copy
Edit
tools.pop();
console.log(tools); // ['Playwright']
✅ shift() – Remove first item
js
Copy
Edit
const data = ['A', 'B', 'C'];
data.shift(); // removes 'A'
console.log(data); // ['B', 'C']
✅ unshift() – Add to beginning
js
Copy
Edit
data.unshift('Z');
console.log(data); // ['Z', 'B', 'C']
✅ forEach() – Loop through array
js
Copy
Edit
const names = ['Adi', 'Mounica'];
names.forEach((name) => {
  console.log(name); // Adi \n Mounica
});
🧪 In Automation: Loop through list items

js
Copy
Edit
const items = ['#name', '#email'];
items.forEach(async (selector) => {
  await page.fill(selector, 'Test');
});
✅ map() – Return a new array after modifying
js
Copy
Edit
const nums = [1, 2, 3];
const doubled = nums.map((n) => n * 2);
console.log(doubled); // [2, 4, 6]
✅ filter() – Return a new array with matching condition
js
Copy
Edit
const numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
const even = numbers.filter((n) => n % 2 === 0);
console.log(even); // [2, 4]
✅ find() – Return the first match
js
Copy
Edit
const users = [
  { name: 'Adi', role: 'QA' },
  { name: 'Suman', role: 'Dev' }
];
const qa = users.find((u) => u.role === 'QA');
console.log(qa); // { name: 'Adi', role: 'QA' }
✅ includes() – Check if value exists
js
Copy
Edit
const skills = ['JavaScript', 'Playwright'];
console.log(skills.includes('Playwright')); // true
✅ slice() – Extract portion (non-destructive)
js
Copy
Edit
const tools = ['A', 'B', 'C', 'D'];
console.log(tools.slice(1, 3)); // ['B', 'C']
✅ splice() – Remove/Replace/Add (destructive)
js
Copy
Edit
const items = ['A', 'B', 'C'];
items.splice(1, 1); // remove 1 item at index 1
console.log(items); // ['A', 'C']